Actually, most ATX motherboards provide 3.3V output. The problem is that
they don'y provide ENOUGH 3.3V.
Most ATX power supplies give you about 10 to 15 amps at 3.3V (33 to 50 watts).
The LX at 533MHz needs 75W to be on the safe side. 95W if you are running
it at 600MHz.
The most commonly used PS for the LX is from a company called EMACS, and
are supplied often in cases from Axion.
They can be had, ask dealers for details ( we sell them, for example).

