Subject: Re: Best Linux-alpha scsi controller?
In-Reply-To: <199711241512.KAA25226@mail-out-1.tiac.net>

With regards to your message at 10:12 AM 11-24-97 -0500, Stephen J. Gaudet.
Where you stated:
>May want to look at this a littel closer, Intraserver did some thing so the
>cheaper ITI-3140U will NOT work under Digital UNIX.  Eariler cards this was
>not the case but recent cards this is true.  We tried it, won't work under
>Digital UNIX.
>
>Cheers,
>
>Steve
Hi Steve.
Look closely at the crystal on these. To run on Digital UNIX the 3140U
needs an 80MHz crystal. For NT and Linux it needs 40.
This is supposed to change with 4.0d UNIX.
If you look at the 4140 (SCSI/Ether combo) they even have a jumper on the
card to make the switch. So there IS a separate UNIX 3140 (for now).

